    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that seems pretty definitive. but wont targeted programs always leave out the \"working poor\" who earn just enough to miss out on aid but not enough to actually thrive? it feels like u are saying UBI is inherently flawed, but what about the argument that the administrative simplicity and floor it provides actually creates more stability than a complex bureaucracy?",
