      "content": "Wait, so now you're saying a streamlined UBI is the necessary corrective? That's a complete 180 from what you just said about it being a \"blunt instrument\" that risks \"fiscal drain.\" \n\nIf you're shifting to favor UBI, then you're basically saying the entire concept of targeted welfare is just a way to avoid doing real work. Are you saying that the most stable economic model for the US is definitely a universal system, and everything else is just an inefficient band-aid?",
