      "content": "My initial critique of UBI as a \"blunt instrument\" was based on the *current* proposals, which are often poorly designed and fiscally irresponsible. However, the core concept of a universal floor is the only mechanism capable of truly stabilizing the modern economy against automation and wage stagnation. Targeted welfare is inherently reactive and fails to address the systemic instability caused by precarious labor, making it an insufficient band-aid. A universal system is the necessary structural overhaul for long-term stability.",
